(7480412, 1189607, 140305, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the red, nice shot. I like the processing :)</td>', 'Congrats on the red, nice shot. I like the processing :)', '2016-11-02 00:33:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480413, 1189627, 140305, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Margaret, different to see Iceland in B&amp;W, lovely shot.</td>', 'Congratulations Margaret, different to see Iceland in B&W, lovely shot.', '2016-11-02 00:34:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480414, 1189534, 140305, '<td valign="top">Hey Dennis, congrats on the HM! Beautiful shot and thanks for the link to Karl. Had no idea!</td>', 'Hey Dennis, congrats on the HM! Beautiful shot and thanks for the link to Karl. Had no idea!', '2016-11-02 00:35:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480415, 1189652, 140305, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the HM Janine. How wonderful to be in Paris, beautiful photo!</td>', 'Congrats on the HM Janine. How wonderful to be in Paris, beautiful photo!', '2016-11-02 00:36:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480430, 1189568, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>This looks an interesting location with the chimney forming a key part and influencing your choice of composition. I like the mono conversion though personally I think there is scope to make it a little darker throughout to give it a bit more body. The side lighting on the facing building enhances the textures of the brickwork nicely and the trees are quite vibrant too. A commendable job, well done Jonathon.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge This looks an interesting location with the chimney forming a key part and influencing your choice of composition. I like the mono conversion though personally I think there is scope to make it a little darker throughout to give it a bit more body. The side lighting on the facing building enhances the textures of the brickwork nicely and the trees are quite vibrant too. A commendable job, well done Jonathon.', '2016-11-02 06:32:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480431, 1189627, 135744, '<td valign="top">Congrats Margaret. I thought I recognised that view and realise it is the view of a photo that beat me in this competition:)<br/> <br/><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/travel/gallery/2016/nov/01/readers-travel-photography-competition-october-the-winners" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">https://www.theguardian.com/travel/gallery/2016/nov/01/readers-travel-photography-competition-october-the-winners</a></td>', 'Congrats Margaret. I thought I recognised that view and realise it is the view of a photo that beat me in this competition:) https://www.theguardian.com/travel/gallery/2016/nov/01/readers-travel-photography-competition-october-the-winners', '2016-11-02 06:37:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480434, 1189678, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>What a lovely interesting building this is. Im not sure about the bench, this is a conscious choice you have made to make your image more unique and give it a somewhat quirky feel but it doesnt really work for me to be honest, I would have preferred the plain grassy expanse. The lighting is good in the way it is bringing out all the interesting detail in the front facade.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge What a lovely interesting building this is. Im not sure about the bench, this is a conscious choice you have made to make your image more unique and give it a somewhat quirky feel but it doesnt really work for me to be honest, I would have preferred the plain grassy expanse. The lighting is good in the way it is bringing out all the interesting detail in the front facade.', '2016-11-02 06:50:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480435, 1189607, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Aliaa. This is so beautifully done.</td>', 'Congratulations, Aliaa. This is so beautifully done.', '2016-11-02 06:57:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480436, 1189652, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congrats Janine. This is lovely - a great job with every aspect of shooting and processing.</td>', 'Congrats Janine. This is lovely - a great job with every aspect of shooting and processing.', '2016-11-02 07:00:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480437, 1189631, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>The pier is indeed a notable landmark that blends in well with the tones of the pier itself and those of the sunset and its reflection in the water. The composition of such a shot is determined by the structure itself and leaves little room for anything really creative apart from using the lower third, as you have done, but Im sort of wondering how it would have looked using the upper third with water dominating the lower half as opposed to the rather bland sky. It all feels rather deserted though I can see its not, I think waiting for a person walking their dog into the frame from the right would have livened it up too. Sorry for the lack of comments during the challenge Fabio, I hope this makes up for it.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge The pier is indeed a notable landmark that blends in well with the tones of the pier itself and those of the sunset and its reflection in the water. The composition of such a shot is determined by the structure itself and leaves little room for anything really creative apart from using the lower third, as you have done, but Im sort of wondering how it would have looked using the upper third with water dominating the lower half as opposed to the rather bland sky. It all feels rather deserted though I can see its not, I think waiting for a person walking their dog into the frame from the right would have livened it up too. Sorry for the lack of comments during the challenge Fabio, I hope this makes up for it.', '2016-11-02 07:02:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480438, 1189652, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Most appropriate to choose one of the most famous landmarks in the world! This unusual composition is a refreshing change from the normal compositions we often see, it feels much more dynamic with the people and the bird. Its a shame there wasnt some level of water in the base of the structure to perfectly reflect the tower though I do like the subtle suggestion of reflection we have here. The tower with its head in the clouds helps to accentuate its height making it even more grandiose. Congratulations Janine on the high score and placing.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge Most appropriate to choose one of the most famous landmarks in the world! This unusual composition is a refreshing change from the normal compositions we often see, it feels much more dynamic with the people and the bird. Its a shame there wasnt some level of water in the base of the structure to perfectly reflect the tower though I do like the subtle suggestion of reflection we have here. The tower with its head in the clouds helps to accentuate its height making it even more grandiose. Congratulations Janine on the high score and placing.', '2016-11-02 07:12:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480458, 1189611, 147247, '<td valign="top">Stunning photo! Congrats on the Blue!</td>', 'Stunning photo! Congrats on the Blue!', '2016-11-02 09:44:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480483, 1189611, 183150, '<td valign="top">This is the kind of beautiful photo that would make me want to go immediately to wherever it was taken.  Congrats!</td>', 'This is the kind of beautiful photo that would make me want to go immediately to wherever it was taken.  Congrats!', '2016-11-02 11:37:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480484, 1189638, 183073, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the feedback and votes everybody.  I agree with the comments, when I first processed this there was a bit of detail in the building, enough to make out some texture in the trees and the pillars of the building.  Unfortunately my shots seem to show up quite a bit darker on other peoples devices so it got a bit heavier (great description, BTW), going to have to do some more adjusting to my monitor to get consistency.  The hot spot of the sun was intentional, figured the light would balance with the dark, although I would have preferred it to be slightly more to the right.  Still trying to figure out sharpening and noise reduction, so will work on those halos.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for the feedback and votes everybody.  I agree with the comments, when I first processed this there was a bit of detail in the building, enough to make out some texture in the trees and the pillars of the building.  Unfortunately my shots seem to show up quite a bit darker on other peoples devices so it got a bit heavier (great description, BTW), going to have to do some more adjusting to my monitor to get consistency.  The hot spot of the sun was intentional, figured the light would balance with the dark, although I would have preferred it to be slightly more to the right.  Still trying to figure out sharpening and noise reduction, so will work on those halos. ', '2016-11-02 11:41:08.000000', NULL, 0),
