(7480760, 1189534, 14476, '<td valign="top">Grand to see this image, and to see your work on the front page.<br/>Congratulations on your placement.<br/>I''ll never get (well, maybe never get) to Marin in the right condition again, so this is especially happy.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-03 22:39:02.</i></td>', 'Grand to see this image, and to see your work on the front page.Congratulations on your placement.I''ll never get (well, maybe never get) to Marin in the right condition again, so this is especially happy.', '2016-11-03 22:36:29.000000', '2016-11-03 22:39:02.000000', 0),
(7480798, 1189643, 138630, '<td valign="top">Save first.  Then upload.  Then check the upload through preview to see what it will look at.  Then title and submit that.  All of that helps :)</td>', 'Save first.  Then upload.  Then check the upload through preview to see what it will look at.  Then title and submit that.  All of that helps :)', '2016-11-03 23:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480986, 1189607, 182284, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I gave a 10 on this one it is so refreshing to see something different. The lighting and colors were right on the mark. My Fave.</td>', 'Congratulations! I gave a 10 on this one it is so refreshing to see something different. The lighting and colors were right on the mark. My Fave.', '2016-11-04 15:52:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7480988, 1189611, 182284, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I gave a 10 on this one. You caught her in all her glory. Super Job!</td>', 'Congratulations! I gave a 10 on this one. You caught her in all her glory. Super Job!', '2016-11-04 15:54:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481053, 1189653, 115814, '<td valign="top">This was a 7 from me, Penny. Had I looked more carefully, I''d have seen the title mix-up, but it played no part in my scoring. I love the processing in general, but admit to being among those in opposition to borders. I also think the vignettes in upper left and lower right might be toned down a bit, but this is all largely irrelevant personal preferences. The overall impact of this shot is powerful and makes effective use of tilting.</td>', 'This was a 7 from me, Penny. Had I looked more carefully, I''d have seen the title mix-up, but it played no part in my scoring. I love the processing in general, but admit to being among those in opposition to borders. I also think the vignettes in upper left and lower right might be toned down a bit, but this is all largely irrelevant personal preferences. The overall impact of this shot is powerful and makes effective use of tilting.', '2016-11-05 03:29:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481072, 1189642, 115814, '<td valign="top">I like the muted color palette, which perfectly reflects the grey weather and represents the "landmark" without idealizing the the scene, There''s a sense of place and surrounding space that''s quite effective. I''m conflicted about the large amount of space to the left of the subject. While it does emphasize the expanse of the valley below, it also reveals the slightly distracting dark foliage and rectangular blocks on the near horizon - I wonder if it might be better to crop the left side in to the point of losing the darker objects.</td>', 'I like the muted color palette, which perfectly reflects the grey weather and represents the "landmark" without idealizing the the scene, There''s a sense of place and surrounding space that''s quite effective. I''m conflicted about the large amount of space to the left of the subject. While it does emphasize the expanse of the valley below, it also reveals the slightly distracting dark foliage and rectangular blocks on the near horizon - I wonder if it might be better to crop the left side in to the point of losing the darker objects.', '2016-11-05 12:19:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481098, 1189676, 115814, '<td valign="top">This is really lovely, Neil. I was one of your modal votes of 6. An interesting tableau that''s well composed and provide a great sense of place. I wish the barn was more isolated as the subject somehow. Perhaps by selective lightening use of the radial filter in LR. The greens also appear to be a bit strongly saturated for my eyes. I''m curious, too, if your POV was purposeful to have the outline of the roof arc on the right side of the barn align with the arc of the hills beyond it.</td>', 'This is really lovely, Neil. I was one of your modal votes of 6. An interesting tableau that''s well composed and provide a great sense of place. I wish the barn was more isolated as the subject somehow. Perhaps by selective lightening use of the radial filter in LR. The greens also appear to be a bit strongly saturated for my eyes. I''m curious, too, if your POV was purposeful to have the outline of the roof arc on the right side of the barn align with the arc of the hills beyond it.', '2016-11-05 17:32:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481280, 1189653, 30982, '<td valign="top">Beautifully edited!!  Just an all around great shot, in my opinion.</td>', 'Beautifully edited!!  Just an all around great shot, in my opinion.', '2016-11-07 00:20:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481314, 1189642, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wbanning:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the muted color palette, which perfectly reflects the grey weather and represents the "landmark" without idealizing the the scene, There''s a sense of place and surrounding space that''s quite effective. I''m conflicted about the large amount of space to the left of the subject. While it does emphasize the expanse of the valley below, it also reveals the slightly distracting dark foliage and rectangular blocks on the near horizon - I wonder if it might be better to crop the left side in to the point of losing the darker objects. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are totally spot on about the space to the left. I prefer a tighter crop like a previous entry I had of the same subject:)<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1088136" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1826/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1088136.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1826/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1088136.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1826/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1088136.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by wbanning: I like the muted color palette, which perfectly reflects the grey weather and represents the "landmark" without idealizing the the scene, There''s a sense of place and surrounding space that''s quite effective. I''m conflicted about the large amount of space to the left of the subject. While it does emphasize the expanse of the valley below, it also reveals the slightly distracting dark foliage and rectangular blocks on the near horizon - I wonder if it might be better to crop the left side in to the point of losing the darker objects.   You are totally spot on about the space to the left. I prefer a tighter crop like a previous entry I had of the same subject:) ', '2016-11-07 04:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
